Chapter: DceReach

   dce-doubled   reached as a VALUE -- its address is taken and passed,
                 and it is called through that value. This is the
                 check-func-addr-targets path rather than the call path.
   dce-bump      the same, through a second call site, so the shape is
                 pinned by more than one instance.
   dce-show-tag  reached through a type-class dictionary, which is a
                 record whose field holds the method.

Section: Reached as a value

  dce-doubled : Integer -> Integer
  dce-doubled (n) = n * 2

  dce-bump : Integer -> Integer
  dce-bump (n) = n + 7

  dce-apply-to : (Integer -> Integer), Integer -> Integer
  dce-apply-to (f) (x) = f x

Section: Reached through a dictionary

  class DceTagged where
    dce-show-tag : Integer -> Text

  instance DceTagged Integer where
    dce-show-tag (x) = "tag" & show x

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (dce-apply-to dce-doubled 21))
   print-line-uni (show (dce-apply-to dce-bump 35))
   print-line-uni (dce-show-tag 5)
  end
